        },
        {
          "zh": "ລາວມີໝູ່ສາມຄົນ.",
          "py": "Láao mīi mùu sǎam khon.",
          "tr": {
            "en": "She has three friends."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g03-politeness",
      "level": 1,
      "status": "published",
      "title": {
        "en": "Lao Politeness: Jao, Doey & De",
        "lo": "ຄວາມສຸພາບໃນພາສາລາວ: ເຈົ້າ, ໂດຍ, ເດີ"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Lao culture places deep emphasis on warmth and courtesy. 'ເຈົ້າ' (jao) is used as a polite 'yes' or acknowledgment. 'ໂດຍ' (doey) is formal and shows deep respect (used with elders, monks, officials). Sentence-ending particles like 'ເດີ' (de) soften statements warmly: ສະບາຍດີເດີ, ໂຊກດີເດີ (good luck!).",
        "lo": "ວັດທະນະທຳລາວເນັ້ນຄວາມອ່ອນຫວານສຸພາບ. ຄຳວ່າ 'ໂດຍ' ໃຊ້ຕອບຮັບຜູ້ໃຫຍ່ດ້ວຍຄວາມເຄົາລົບ, 'ເຈົ້າ' ໃຊ້ທົ່ວໄປ, ສ່ວນ 'ເດີ' ເຮັດໃຫ້ປະໂຫຍກອ່ອນໂຍນເປັນກັນເອງ."
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "zh": "ໂດຍ, ຂອບໃຈຫຼາຍໆ.",
          "py": "Dōoei, khɔ̀ɔp-jái lǎai lǎai.",
          "tr": {
            "en": "Yes, thank you very much."
          }
        },
        {
          "zh": "ພົບກັນໃໝ່ເດີ.",
          "py": "Phóp kan mǎi də̂ə.",
          "tr": {
            "en": "See you again soon!"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dialogues": [
    {
      "id": "d01-restaurant",
      "title": {
        "en": "At a Lao Noodle Shop",
        "lo": "ຢູ່ຮ້ານເຝີ"
      },
      "lines": [
        {
          "sp": "Customer",
          "zh": "ສະບາຍດີ, ມີເຝີບໍ?",
          "py": "Sà-bāai-dī, mīi fə̌ə bɔ̀ɔ?",
          "tr": {
            "en": "Hello, do you have pho noodles?"
          }
        },
        {
          "sp": "Vendor",
          "zh": "ໂດຍ, ມີ. ເຈົ້າຢາກກິນເຝີງົວ ຫຼື ເຝີໄກ່?",
          "py": "Dōoei, mīi. Jâo yàak kin fə̌ə ngúaa lɯ̌ɯ fə̌ə kái?",
          "tr": {
            "en": "Yes, we do. Would you like beef pho or chicken pho?"
          }
        },
        {
          "sp": "Customer",
          "zh": "ຂໍເຝີງົວໜຶ່ງຖ້ວຍ ແລະ ນ້ຳດື່ມໜຶ່ງແກ້ວ.",
          "py": "Khɔ̌ɔ fə̌ə ngúaa nɯ̀ng thùai lɛ́ nâm dɯ̀ɯm nɯ̀ng kɛ̂ɛo.",
          "tr": {
            "en": "One bowl of beef pho and one bottle of water, please."
          }
        },
        {
          "sp": "Vendor",
          "zh": "ໂດຍ, ລໍຖ້າໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງເດີ.",
          "py": "Dōoei, lɔɔ thâa nɔ̂ɔi nɯ̀ng də̂ə.",
          "tr": {
            "en": "Certainly, please wait a moment."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d02-market",
      "title": {
        "en": "Bargaining at Talat Sao",
        "lo": "ຊື້ເສື້ອຢູ່ຕະຫຼາດເຊົ້າ"
      },
      "lines": [
        {
          "sp": "Tourist",
          "zh": "ສະບາຍດີ, ເສື້ອໂຕນີ້ລາຄາເທົ່າໃດ?",
          "py": "Sà-bāai-dī, sɯ̂a dtōo nîi lāa-khāa thào-dài?",
          "tr": {
            "en": "Hello, how much is this shirt?"
          }
        },
        {
          "sp": "Seller",
          "zh": "ແປດສິບພັນກີບເດີ.",
          "py": "Pàaet síp phán kìip də̂ə.",
          "tr": {
            "en": "Eighty thousand Kip."
          }
        },
        {
          "sp": "Tourist",
          "zh": "ແພງໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງ, ຫຼຸດໄດ້ບໍ? ເຈັດສິບພັນໄດ້ບໍ?",
          "py": "Pháaeng nɔ̂ɔi nɯ̀ng, lùt dài bɔ̀ɔ? Jét síp phán dài bɔ̀ɔ?",
          "tr": {
            "en": "A little bit expensive, can you discount? How about 70,000 Kip?"
          }
        },
        {
          "sp": "Seller",
          "zh": "ໄດ້, ຂອບໃຈຫຼາຍໆເດີ!",
          "py": "Dài, khɔ̀ɔp-jái lǎai lǎai də̂ə!",
          "tr": {
            "en": "Can do! Thank you very much!"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
